# Physics receipt: Density on the old page, through the panel. Its signature
# is room following mass (the rank of mass against area share) and an even
# density, not energy (the flow writes positions). Springs is the negative
# control, and picking Density disables the overlays with the law's reason.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
assert snap ready == true
dom click [data-command="toggle-physics"]
settle 1
assert snap physics-paused == false
# No arrangement: the boot Spiral's anchor springs would pull under every law.
select #gs-arrangement-select free
dom click [data-command="apply-arrangement"]
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
# The control: Springs does not give room by mass.
select #gs-physics-select spring.rapier
dom click [data-command="apply-physics"]
settle 300
assert snap physics-law == spring.rapier
assert snap layout-mass-area-rank <= 0.79
# An overlay ticked under Springs is disabled once Density is picked.
check #gs-overlay-tide on
assert attr #gs-overlay-note hidden
select #gs-physics-select density.gastner-newman
settle 1
assert attr #gs-physics-overlays disabled
assert dom #gs-overlay-note Density takes no overlays
capture physics_density_refused
wait
dom click [data-command="apply-physics"]
settle 1
assert snap physics-law == density.gastner-newman
assert snap physics-profile == law.density
assert dom #gs-product-status Physics set to Density
capture physics_density_start
wait
# Until the flow stops (three calm passes, the 120-pass cap behind them;
# one tick a frame here).
settle 2400
assert snap physics-continuous == false
capture physics_density_settled
wait
assert snap layout-mass-area-rank >= 0.8
assert snap layout-density-cv <= 0.35
assert snap layout-overlaps == 0
log physics density receipt complete
